# =============================================================================
# Cloudflare Worker — local secrets template (SPEC section 32)
#
# Copy to `.dev.vars` for local development:
#     cp apps/worker/.dev.vars.example apps/worker/.dev.vars
#
# `.dev.vars` is GITIGNORED: .gitignore ignores `.dev.vars` and `.dev.vars.*`
# and re-includes only this `.example` file. Never commit real secrets.
#
# ONLY SECRETS BELONG HERE. Non-secret Worker configuration lives in
# `wrangler.jsonc` under `vars` / `env.<env>.vars` and is committed on purpose:
#   X402_NETWORK, X402_RECIPIENT, X402_FACILITATOR_URL, X402_PRICE_USD,
#   BACKEND_ORIGIN_URL, and the dev-only DEV_BYPASS_PAYMENT flag.
#
# This file is read by `wrangler dev`. It has NO effect on a deployed Worker:
# remotely, secrets are set once with
#     npx wrangler secret put BACKEND_AUTH_SECRET
#
# PLACEHOLDERS ONLY. Do not put a real secret in this file.
# =============================================================================

# Shared server-to-server secret, identical to the backend's BACKEND_AUTH_SECRET
# in your local `.env`. The Worker sends it as the `x-backend-auth` header and
# the backend rejects any mismatch (SPEC section 14).
# Generate one with:   openssl rand -hex 32
BACKEND_AUTH_SECRET=
